---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import UiLabel from "../../components/UiLabel.astro";
import HelpCard from "../../components/HelpCard.astro";

// Issue #1106: ownership transfer gets its own short guide (issue #4's
// parent-to-child handover). The mechanics are the in-app help card
// rendered from the export; role names and buttons come from the ARB
// through <UiLabel>; every factual claim carries a `<!-- cite: ... -->`
// ledger entry checked by `site/scripts/check-claims.mjs`.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Transferring ownership"
  description="How ownership transfer works: a one-way handover of a profile to its subject's own account, with every past entry's original attribution kept."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1 class="doc__title">Transferring ownership</h1>
    <p class="doc__lede">
      A profile created by a parent does not have to stay hers. When the
      person it is about is ready — Maya turning sixteen, say — ownership
      moves to her account in one step, and the parent chooses how, or
      whether, to stay on.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>What a transfer is</h2>
      <HelpCard id="ownership-transfer" />
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Before the handover</h2>
      <p>
        Transfer is deliberate and one-way — there is no undo, only a new
        transfer back. A few things to know first:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The transfer does not move data anywhere: the profile and every
          entry in it stay exactly where they are. What changes is who the
          account that owns it is, and with it the
          <UiLabel key="guardianRoleLabelPrimaryGuardian" /> seat.
          <!-- cite: lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (ownershipTransfer card); lib/domain/sharing/ownership_transfer_service.dart -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Attribution never changes: every past entry keeps whoever
          originally logged it, so the record Dana kept during Maya's
          early days stays marked as Dana's.
          <!-- cite: lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (ownershipTransfer card); lib/ui/sharing/claim_profile_sheet.dart (claimProfileBody) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          If the new owner later deletes her account, this profile's
          history goes with it — worth a conversation before arming the
          transfer.
          <!-- cite: lib/l10n/app_en.arb (sharingTransferOwnershipBulletDeleteAccount); lib/ui/sharing/transfer_ownership_screen.dart -->
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The parent's side</h2>
      <ol class="doc__steps">
        <li>
          Open the profile's guardian management and choose
          <UiLabel key="manageGuardiansTransferOwnershipTooltip" />. Only
          the profile's <UiLabel key="guardianRoleLabelPrimaryGuardian" />
          can arm a transfer.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/transfer_ownership_screen.dart; lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (ownershipTransfer card) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Choose the role you keep. The two offers, in the app's words:
          <UiLabel key="transferOwnershipRoleCoParent" /> or
          <UiLabel key="transferOwnershipRoleViewer" />. Afterwards that
          access is an ordinary membership — the new owner can change or
          remove it at any time.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/transfer_ownership_screen.dart (continuing-role choice, transferOwnershipRole*) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Confirm. The app states the handover —
          <UiLabel
            key="transferOwnershipConfirmBody"
            values={{ name: "Maya", role: "Co-Parent" }}
          />
          — and creates a single-use link that expires after 72 hours.
          Send it to Maya; the pending transfer shows as
          <UiLabel key="manageGuardiansWaitingForRedemption" /> until she
          claims it.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/transfer_ownership_screen.dart (confirm body, 72h link); lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (ownershipTransfer card) -->
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Maya's side</h2>
      <ol class="doc__steps">
        <li>
          Maya opens the link on her own device, signed in to her own
          account. The claim screen explains it:
          <UiLabel key="claimProfileBody" />
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/claim_profile_sheet.dart (claimProfileBody) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          She confirms with
          <UiLabel key="claimProfileBecomeGuardianAction" />. Ownership and
          the primary-guardian seat move to her account in one step; Dana
          keeps the role she chose, from then on as an ordinary guardian.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/claim_profile_sheet.dart; lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (ownershipTransfer card) -->
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        That is the whole ceremony. Nothing about Maya's log changes on
        the surface — same history, same estimates — and the family keeps
        sharing it exactly as before, now with its subject as its owner.
        <!-- cite: docs/product/positioning.md (ownership can move with the family); lib/domain/sharing/ownership_transfer_service.dart -->
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
